{
    "word": "agnathous",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "9409a298-cc24-380c-a68f-0cfc024e4753",
                "word": "agnathous",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cd3245af-bbf9-3011-a4a8-2998b46b7ec1",
                        "entry_id": "9409a298-cc24-380c-a68f-0cfc024e4753",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Jawless."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "39f9f044-c65d-4bee-8dcc-1d922d66ec2f",
                                "sense_id": "cd3245af-bbf9-3011-a4a8-2998b46b7ec1",
                                "text": "The Onchidiidæ are described as agnathous, but I am confident of having observed the jaw figured."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c99a221b-e3a2-40fa-8b48-9973f43fcb92",
                                "sense_id": "cd3245af-bbf9-3011-a4a8-2998b46b7ec1",
                                "text": "The mouth is a transverse slit, which shows no teeth, nor any jaws properly so called, and therefore affords an apparent support to the agnathous theory of the Ostracodermi."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "768a0143-7cce-4f7b-a504-886483a276ba",
                                "sense_id": "cd3245af-bbf9-3011-a4a8-2998b46b7ec1",
                                "text": "This and related agnathous (jawless), finless forms inhabited shallow seas or estuarine habitats[…]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7c080ae5-eba8-42c6-bbee-95b519175cb1",
                                "sense_id": "cd3245af-bbf9-3011-a4a8-2998b46b7ec1",
                                "text": "Parenthetically, this line treatment suggests an attempt to mimic the agnathous (jawless) head, if we suppose that the jaw area was colored suitably dark in contrast to the face proper."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8882574d-7414-3285-9c7e-30067000d771",
                        "entry_id": "9409a298-cc24-380c-a68f-0cfc024e4753",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Afflicted by or characteristic of agnathia."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b15a1937-11b0-4f44-ba79-7839c3ba11e0",
                                "sense_id": "8882574d-7414-3285-9c7e-30067000d771",
                                "text": "Dr Underhill exhibited an agnathous and hydrocephalic fœtus. This was an instance of the rare abnormality due to defect of the lower jaw."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7ebf7139-a920-4046-84a6-1cf9f2bf5069",
                                "sense_id": "8882574d-7414-3285-9c7e-30067000d771",
                                "text": "Upon this view an agnathous fœtus may be regarded as sometimes due to a posterior dichotomy, which has ultimately become a complete separation, and in which the two fœtuses have developed equally during a considerable part of intra-uterine life."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "86865ce8-3599-42b5-92dc-7150a0702f2b",
                                "sense_id": "8882574d-7414-3285-9c7e-30067000d771",
                                "text": "In all the neonates examined from the partially agnathous strain, there was no obvious agenesia of the lower mandible."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
